body:
Execute Ticket 2 (t-run2-w2-policy-guard) for Release Audit Run 2.

IMPORTANT HEADLESS WORKER RULES:
- Use ONLY view_file, replace_file_content, and write_to_file.
- Do NOT call run_command (the scheduler automatically runs the test suite in the gating phase immediately after you finish editing).
- Only edit files in your declared scope: hooks/policy/shell.mjs, hooks/policy/evaluate.mjs, test/pre-tool-use.test.mjs, test/policy-guard-bypass.test.mjs.

1. In hooks/policy/evaluate.mjs (SHOULD-FIX #4 & BACKLOG #3):
   - Note: isWithin(child, parent, platform) in hooks/policy/paths.mjs returns true when child is equal to or inside parent.
   - In containsProtected(r, ctx) (around lines 212-217), r is the directory being deleted/moved (parent) and repo.root is the ADLC repository root (child). Update the loop over ctx.workspacePaths so it checks both physical (realOr(repo.root) vs r.real) and lexical (repo.root vs r.lexical):
     for (const w of ctx.workspacePaths) {
       const repo = ctx.repoAt(w);
       if (!repo.adlc) continue;
       const repoReal = realOr(repo.root);
       if ((repoReal !== r.real && isWithin(repoReal, r.real, ctx.platform)) ||
           (repo.root !== r.lexical && isWithin(repo.root, r.lexical, ctx.platform))) {
         return deny('Target path contains an ADLC repository');
       }
     }
   - In buildContext(payload, options = {}) (around lines 466-491):
     Hoist const platform = options.platform ?? process.platform; above workspaceRealPaths, compute const workspaceRealPaths = unique(workspacePaths.map((w) => physicalResolve(w, '/', platform).real)); and include workspaceRealPaths on the returned ctx object.

2. In hooks/policy/shell.mjs (SHOULD-FIX #3 & SHOULD-FIX #4):
   - Add physicalResolve to the import from './paths.mjs' at the top of hooks/policy/shell.mjs.
   - In checkDestructiveRoot (around lines 375-379), remember repo.root is child and r is parent:
     for (const repo of ctx.knownRepos()) {
       if (!repo.adlc) continue;
       const repoReal = physicalResolve(repo.root, '/', ctx.platform).real;
       if (isWithin(repoReal, r.real, ctx.platform) || isWithin(repo.root, r.lexical, ctx.platform)) {
         return deny('Target path is an ADLC repository root (or its parent), which holds frozen trust-root state');
       }
     }
   - In classifyLine(line, cwd, ctx, depth) (around lines 476-484):
     const target = dirChangeTarget(sub, current, ctx, cdpath);
     const targetReal = target !== null ? physicalResolve(target, current, ctx.platform).real : null;
     const wsReals = ctx.workspaceRealPaths ?? ctx.workspacePaths.map((w) => physicalResolve(w, '/', ctx.platform).real);
     const intoWorkspace = targetReal !== null && wsReals.some((wReal) => isWithin(targetReal, wReal, ctx.platform));
     if (!(subs.length > 1 && intoWorkspace)) verdicts.push(classifySubcommand(sub, current, ctx, depth));
     current = targetReal;
     continue;
   - In classifyRunCommand(args, ctx) (around lines 495-505):
     const cwdLexical = isAbsolute(cwdRaw) ? resolve(cwdRaw) : resolve(ctx.workspacePaths[0] ?? '/', cwdRaw);
     const cwdReal = physicalResolve(cwdLexical, '/', ctx.platform).real;
     const cwdRepo = ctx.repoAt(cwdReal).adlc ? ctx.repoAt(cwdReal) : ctx.repoAt(cwdLexical);
     const adlcContext = cwdRepo.adlc || ctx.workspacePaths.some((w) => ctx.repoAt(w).adlc);
     const wsReals = ctx.workspaceRealPaths ?? ctx.workspacePaths.map((w) => physicalResolve(w, '/', ctx.platform).real);
     const insideWorkspace = wsReals.some((wReal) => isWithin(cwdReal, wReal, ctx.platform));
     if (adlcContext && (!isAbsolute(cwdRaw) || !insideWorkspace)) {
       return deny('Shell command working directory outside declared workspace paths in an ADLC repository is forbidden');
     }
     return classifyLine(line, cwdReal, ctx, 0);

3. In test/policy-guard-bypass.test.mjs (at the end of the file):
   - Add tests verifying:
     (a) run_command in an ADLC workspace with Cwd pointing to a symlink inside the workspace that resolves outside is denied.
     (b) compound "cd out-link && ls" where out-link points outside the workspace is not treated as intoWorkspace.
     (c) run_command with physical Cwd when workspacePaths uses a symlinked path is allowed.
     (d) rm -rf .. from an ADLC workspace reached via a symlinked ancestor is denied by checkDestructiveRoot, while rm <ordinary-file> inside the repo passes checkDestructiveRoot.
     (e) containsProtected denies deleting the physical parent directory above a symlinked ADLC workspace.
